    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to consider the nature of the collisions and how the cars will collide and collide in terms of the number of cars. Since the cars are moving at the same speed and will only collide when they meet exactly, the number of collisions possible will be simply the number of pairs of half the number of cars.\n\nHere's the implementation of the function:\n\n```python\ndef car_race_collision(n: int) -> int:\n    # The number of collisions is simply the square of the number of cars\n    return n * n\n```\n\nThis function works because each car will collide with every other car exactly once. Therefore, the total number of collisions is the square of the number of cars.",
